      "text": "I've logged execution as UNKNOWN rather than normal, because the growth stage needs a tube pressure reading and this furnace has no pressure gauge.\n\n- **What looks normal:** the temperature is holding at 749.3–749.8 °C against the 750 °C setpoint, after a brief overshoot to 760.6 °C at 2520 s. Heater power (about 44–46%) matches that temperature, and argon flow is on setpoint (99.5–100.3 sccm).\n- **What O2 tells us:** exhaust oxygen came down from about 28,800 ppm during purge to about 3–7 ppm and stayed there. That argues against an air leak.\n- **What we can't check:** without a pressure reading, a blocked exhaust or a pressure drift can't be ruled out. The O2 and argon flow readings wouldn't necessarily show either one.\n\nThere's no sample characterization yet, so there's no evidence either way on whether the material grew. I recommended continuing, because nothing observed is abnormal. A pressure reading would be needed before this run's result can count as a fair test of the recipe."
